<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Billy Hughes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1862–1952</span> · Also known as William Morris Hughes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Billy Hughes was prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> from 1915 to 1923 and led the country through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. His campaign for conscription, rejected in referendums in 1916 and 1917, split the Labor Party and led him to form the Nationalist Party. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-conference-1919-1920">Paris Peace Conference</a> he secured a mandate over German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> and opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s racial equality proposal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/billy-hughes.jpg" alt="Billy Hughes" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fairfax Corporation · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Billy_Hughes_1919.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
